WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.701
- We're back for part two of
our Worth It Taiwan series.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.961
Today, we're doing soup.

00:00:04.961 --> 00:00:06.401
- Taiwan style.

00:00:06.401 --> 00:00:08.524
It's amazing 'cause it's so hot in Taiwan,

00:00:08.524 --> 00:00:10.525
and yet, they love their soup here.

00:00:10.525 --> 00:00:12.240
- It's eaten for breakfast,
lunch and dinner,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.794
so many great dishes to try.

00:00:13.794 --> 00:00:15.117
But before we get there,

00:00:15.117 --> 00:00:16.049
Steven where are we?

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:19.764
- We are here at the Jingzaijiao
Tile-paved Salt Fields.

00:00:19.764 --> 00:00:21.732
Is that right Inga?

00:00:21.732 --> 00:00:22.716
- Jingzaijiao.

00:00:22.716 --> 00:00:23.965
- Historically one of the earliest

00:00:23.965 --> 00:00:25.864
salt-producing areas of Taiwan.

00:00:25.864 --> 00:00:28.401
Ocean water comes in,
the sun evaporates it,

00:00:28.401 --> 00:00:29.381
and you're left with salt.

00:00:29.381 --> 00:00:32.315
Speaking of salty liquids.

00:00:32.315 --> 00:00:33.148
- Sweat?

00:00:33.148 --> 00:00:34.197
- No.
- Oh.

00:00:34.197 --> 00:00:35.030
- We're doing soup.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:35.863
- Today on Worth It,

00:00:35.863 --> 00:00:37.484
we're going to be trying
three Taiwanese soups

00:00:37.484 --> 00:00:39.102
at three drastically
different price points

00:00:39.102 --> 00:00:41.542
to find out which one is the
most worth it at its price.

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:42.461
- It's so windy.

00:00:42.461 --> 00:00:43.866
- The typhoon just passed.

00:00:43.866 --> 00:00:46.101
- We're heading a little bit
north of the city of Tainan

00:00:46.101 --> 00:00:47.326
to where, Inga?

00:00:47.326 --> 00:00:49.370
- We're going to Chiayi
to have some fish soup

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.963
at Lin Cong Ming Yu Tang.

00:00:50.963 --> 00:00:54.800
- Lin is my last name,
and cong ming is smart,

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.918
so we're just going to,
like, the smart version of me

00:00:57.918 --> 00:00:59.203
fish place.
- Oh wow.

00:00:59.203 --> 00:01:01.010
That'll be a extra special treat.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.736
(jazzy music)

00:01:03.736 --> 00:01:04.596
- Taiwan is very hot.

00:01:04.596 --> 00:01:05.429
- Yes.

00:01:05.429 --> 00:01:06.638
- [Steven] Soup is a very hot food.

00:01:06.638 --> 00:01:08.700
Why do Taiwanese people love soup so much?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.950
Taiwan was a poor place.

00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:13.531
It's easier to feel full
adding soup to the meal.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:18.286
We've been serving this soup for the past
60 years, since my grandfather's time.

00:01:18.286 --> 00:01:21.539
What's special about this is we
cook 100 servings in one go.

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:25.043
The taste can only be acquired by using
such big amounts of ingredients.

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:30.840
The essence of the abundant ingredients is
condensed in one bowl of soup.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:32.201
- What kind of fish is in the soup?

00:01:32.201 --> 00:01:36.451
We mainly use silver carp
and salmon in our soup.

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:38.223
Silver carp is a native Taiwanese river fish.

00:01:38.223 --> 00:01:44.729
Our salmon is imported and it's quite
popular among gourmets.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:54.155
Our broth base is made with pork bone and
water, cooking from 8 a.m. until 9 p.m.

00:01:54.155 --> 00:01:58.034
Meanwhile, preparing the rest of the ingredients.

00:01:58.034 --> 00:01:58.827
Napa cabbage

00:01:58.827 --> 00:01:59.786
Garlic

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:00.912
Onion

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:01.830
Scallion

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:02.872
Non-GMO tofu

00:02:02.872 --> 00:02:10.171
Next step is chopping up the
fish and deep-frying them.

00:02:10.252 --> 00:02:14.113
Why is the fish fried and
then added afterwards?

00:02:14.113 --> 00:02:18.363
There was no refrigerating to preserve
the fish back then in Taiwan.

00:02:19.347 --> 00:02:23.518
My grandpa opted for deep-
frying to dehydrate the fish.

00:02:23.518 --> 00:02:27.939
It also helps to absorb the broth
when submerged in the soup.

00:02:28.174 --> 00:02:30.648
I noticed that customers can
come back with their bowls

00:02:30.648 --> 00:02:31.810
and get more broth.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:33.570
It's a tradition of the restaurant.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:37.574
We strive to treat our customers like family.
You should eat to your heart's content at home.

00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:42.662
It's also thanks to the continuous support of our customers
that we can cook in such great quantity.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:45.957
That allows a continuous flow
of soup for everyone to share.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.643
(cash register dings)

00:02:48.643 --> 00:02:49.476
- Ooh!

00:02:49.476 --> 00:02:50.836
- Oh...

00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:52.378
Yay...

00:02:52.378 --> 00:02:53.260
(Steven speaks in foreign language)

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.436
- What's the plate for?

00:02:54.436 --> 00:02:56.023
- For the fish bone.

00:02:56.023 --> 00:02:57.620
- Oh, fish bones.
- Oh...

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:58.744
- Is this your beer?

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:00.657
- Yes, it's my fish beer.

00:03:00.657 --> 00:03:01.490
- Cheers, Steven.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.687
(bottles clink)

00:03:02.687 --> 00:03:04.952
(trumpet music)

00:03:04.952 --> 00:03:06.413
Look at that logo.

00:03:06.413 --> 00:03:09.391
Fish soup beer, I am blown away.

00:03:09.391 --> 00:03:11.946
- Cheers in Mandarin is...

00:03:11.946 --> 00:03:13.127
(Steven speaks in foreign language)

00:03:13.127 --> 00:03:14.121
Is that right?

00:03:14.121 --> 00:03:17.315
(Andrew speaks in foreign language)

00:03:17.315 --> 00:03:20.065
- Okay, that was very unexpected.

00:03:21.232 --> 00:03:22.457
Wow, again.

00:03:22.457 --> 00:03:24.457
- Wow, a thousand times.

00:03:25.362 --> 00:03:26.428
- This is very refreshing.

00:03:26.428 --> 00:03:27.261
- It is.

00:03:27.261 --> 00:03:29.428
- Give me one word.

00:03:29.428 --> 00:03:30.261
- Wow.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.349
- [Steven] So this is the
marquis piece right here.

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:36.502
I'm just gonna bite into this.

00:03:36.502 --> 00:03:37.588
(Andrew groans in satisfaction)

00:03:37.588 --> 00:03:39.100
- This is like a dish that dares you

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.296
to want something else.

00:03:40.296 --> 00:03:41.320
You want vegetables?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.153
Boom, we got it.

00:03:42.153 --> 00:03:42.986
You want tofu?

00:03:42.986 --> 00:03:43.819
Forget about it.

00:03:43.819 --> 00:03:44.652
You want pork?

00:03:44.652 --> 00:03:45.485
We got it right here.

00:03:45.485 --> 00:03:46.442
You want fish? Boom.

00:03:46.442 --> 00:03:47.957
Fry it? We can do it.

00:03:47.957 --> 00:03:49.573
- Yeah, when she was
listing the ingredients,

00:03:49.573 --> 00:03:51.509
it was just like the NBA All-Star Game.

00:03:51.509 --> 00:03:54.096
And here we have the tofu!

00:03:54.096 --> 00:03:55.947
Next up, cabbage!

00:03:55.947 --> 00:03:57.126
- Y'all ready for this?

00:03:57.126 --> 00:03:57.959
(Steven laughs)

00:03:57.959 --> 00:04:02.376
Chiayi is also very famous for
turkey meat sauce over rice.

00:04:00.823 --> 00:04:05.119
Customers always get the combo of
turkey rice and fish head soup in here.

00:04:05.042 --> 00:04:06.398
Turkey rice.

00:04:06.398 --> 00:04:09.095
I love how this soup,
with all of this stuff,

00:04:09.095 --> 00:04:09.928
they were like,

00:04:09.928 --> 00:04:11.568
"Nah, you still need some turkey rice."

00:04:11.568 --> 00:04:12.401
- That's right.

00:04:12.401 --> 00:04:13.933
If there's one thing we
learned here in Taiwan,

00:04:13.933 --> 00:04:15.468
you cannot leave a restaurant hungry.

00:04:15.468 --> 00:04:17.164
They will assault you with food.

00:04:17.164 --> 00:04:18.657
In the most lovingly way possible.

00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:19.690
- Yeah.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.753
(upbeat music)

00:04:21.753 --> 00:04:25.983
Mm, it's just turkey meat
and fat on a bowl of rice.

00:04:25.983 --> 00:04:26.816
It's great.

00:04:26.816 --> 00:04:28.457
If you weren't an adventurous eater,

00:04:28.457 --> 00:04:31.207
this would seem like a scary bowl of food,

00:04:31.207 --> 00:04:34.746
but it all just kind of
blends into this big soft hug.

00:04:34.746 --> 00:04:35.579
I don't know.

00:04:35.579 --> 00:04:36.478
It tastes nice.

00:04:36.478 --> 00:04:38.110
It's a kind taste.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.213
- That's exactly how you
say it in Mandarin though.

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.290
- Really?
- Good eat, right?

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.521
Good taste.

00:04:42.521 --> 00:04:44.145
(Inga speaks in foreign language)

00:04:44.145 --> 00:04:47.000
- Means good eat, good taste, yeah.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.440
- Let's spread the kindness.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:49.425
(Andrew slaps hand on table)

00:04:49.425 --> 00:04:50.824
- Once I finish this meal,

00:04:50.824 --> 00:04:53.485
it will be so long until
I get to eat this again.

00:04:53.485 --> 00:04:54.522
And that makes me sad.

00:04:54.522 --> 00:04:56.691
- I know, this whole
trip is actually just--

00:04:56.691 --> 00:04:58.691
- It's sad.
- The worst.

00:05:01.026 --> 00:05:01.982
(Inga speaks in foreign language)

00:05:05.982 --> 00:05:08.342
- That soup was incredible.

00:05:08.342 --> 00:05:11.305
In the rainbow of soup to stew,

00:05:11.305 --> 00:05:14.281
this was somewhere in
the middle in like the--

00:05:14.281 --> 00:05:15.375
- Stoup?
- Stoup

00:05:15.375 --> 00:05:16.363
section, yeah.
- There it is!

00:05:16.363 --> 00:05:18.094
- So before we get to our next soup,

00:05:18.094 --> 00:05:19.657
we decided to get some treats

00:05:19.657 --> 00:05:21.689
at the Garden Night Market in Tainan.

00:05:21.689 --> 00:05:24.820
- [Steven] This is my favorite
treat at Night Market.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.042
It is a peanut roll with
ice cream and cilantro.

00:05:28.042 --> 00:05:28.875
- [Andrew] What?

00:05:28.875 --> 00:05:30.065
Cilantro in a dessert?

00:05:30.065 --> 00:05:30.909
I guess it makes sense,

00:05:30.909 --> 00:05:32.262
we put mint in desserts,

00:05:32.262 --> 00:05:33.241
and that's just

00:05:33.241 --> 00:05:34.587
another green leaf.
- Oh, I didn't even

00:05:34.587 --> 00:05:35.532
think of that.

00:05:35.532 --> 00:05:36.949
Cheers?
- Cheers.

00:05:40.587 --> 00:05:41.728
- [Steven] Huh?

00:05:41.728 --> 00:05:42.561
Huh?
- Oh.

00:05:43.774 --> 00:05:44.955
Huh?
- Oh.

00:05:44.955 --> 00:05:46.910
I like dessert cilantro.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.458
So our next soup is actually
going to be hot pot.

00:05:49.458 --> 00:05:50.291
- Hot pot fact!

00:05:50.291 --> 00:05:53.951
- Archeologists have found pots
from two thousand years ago

00:05:53.951 --> 00:05:56.317
that may have been used
to make an early iteration

00:05:56.317 --> 00:05:57.150
of hot pot.

00:05:57.150 --> 00:06:00.695
These were found in the
Anhui province of China.

00:06:00.695 --> 00:06:02.253
- Wow, old hot pot.

00:06:02.253 --> 00:06:03.611
Dude, hot pot for me,

00:06:03.611 --> 00:06:05.776
every Thanksgiving in the Lin family,

00:06:05.776 --> 00:06:08.320
we always, always, always eat hot pot.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:09.623
- It would make sense that soup was one

00:06:09.623 --> 00:06:11.435
of the oldest things humans ate.

00:06:11.435 --> 00:06:14.898
- Yeah just water, throw some
stuff in there and eat it.

00:06:14.898 --> 00:06:17.011
- Tomorrow, hot pot.

00:06:17.011 --> 00:06:18.202
Inga where are we going?

00:06:18.202 --> 00:06:20.146
- We are going to A Yu Niu Rou Sha Sha Guo

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.177
to eat some beef soup.

00:06:22.177 --> 00:06:23.312
- That's what I'm talking about.

00:06:23.312 --> 00:06:24.627
Beef soup.

00:06:24.627 --> 00:06:26.887
Get that hot pot, throw
some beef in there,

00:06:26.887 --> 00:06:28.902
throw some soup in there,
throw some veggies in there.

00:06:28.902 --> 00:06:30.473
Whatever you want, we're gonna eat it.

00:06:30.473 --> 00:06:31.306
(Steven coughs)

00:06:31.306 --> 00:06:32.520
Excuse me.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:34.270
I choked on a peanut.

00:06:35.744 --> 00:06:37.622
Why do you love hot pot so much?

00:06:37.438 --> 00:06:42.485
Life is perfect while you enjoy this
pot of delicious broth and beef.

00:06:42.485 --> 00:06:46.864
Room temperature beef shabu-shabu
is known for its freshness.

00:06:46.864 --> 00:06:50.910
The cattle are raised in the
mountains all over Taiwan.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.955
Then butchered in the government-run
slaughterhouse in the Shanhua District of Tainan.

00:06:53.955 --> 00:06:56.582
The beef comes straight from there
after being butchered and inspected.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:58.280
- How often do you get the deliveries?

00:06:58.280 --> 00:06:59.113
Every meal.

00:06:59.113 --> 00:06:59.946
Every meal?

00:07:00.128 --> 00:07:02.505
For example, the beef served now during
lunch was butchered this morning.

00:07:02.505 --> 00:07:06.801
Therefore the beef has this natural
sweetness and QQ (chewy) texture.

00:07:08.332 --> 00:07:10.727
We saw that it arrived by taxi.

00:07:10.727 --> 00:07:12.325
Is it always come by taxi?

00:07:12.325 --> 00:07:17.325
We paid the cab to pick it up because
we're too busy in the store.

00:07:17.494 --> 00:07:20.340
That's so cool, the meat
takes a cab to every meal.

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:21.898
(everybody laughing)

00:07:21.898 --> 00:07:25.111
It takes about 6-8 hours to make the broth.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.904
The first layer of ingredients is beef bones.

00:07:26.904 --> 00:07:30.324
Second layer is stacks of beef brisket.

00:07:30.324 --> 00:07:32.952
We use about 264 pounds of brisket for the broth.

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:37.165
Topping the pot with one bag of
vegetables and fruits each.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.816
There's also vegetables
in the dish already?

00:07:39.816 --> 00:07:42.503
The vegetables in the small pot is to
bring out the taste of the broth.

00:07:42.503 --> 00:07:43.796
Cabbage is the star of the pot.

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:48.968
The vegetables really complement the
broth and make the hot pot perfect.

00:07:49.161 --> 00:07:51.537
For someone who's never
had hot pot before,

00:07:51.537 --> 00:07:52.836
how do you eat it?

00:07:52.836 --> 00:07:56.225
Dip the beef in the boiling soup around
3 times/5 seconds and it's ready to eat.

00:07:56.225 --> 00:07:59.395
I always recommend eating without condiments first.

00:07:59.395 --> 00:08:02.398
For the second bite, try the beef with
a bit of our special sauce.

00:08:05.943 --> 00:08:11.032
My husband is in charge of extracting
the prime cut out of the beef.

00:08:11.032 --> 00:08:16.579
The freshly butchered beef is quite soft and
requires great skills with the knife.

00:08:16.579 --> 00:08:21.292
He is so good with the knife! Every piece
comes out with the same thickness!

00:08:21.187 --> 00:08:23.127
You also have this pork rice.

00:08:23.127 --> 00:08:25.136
It's free for all the customers?

00:08:25.136 --> 00:08:27.215
My husband is a generous guy.

00:08:27.215 --> 00:08:30.760
He wants the customers to have the rice to
go with the delicious beef shabu-shabu.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:31.844
Perfect combination!

00:08:32.946 --> 00:08:34.198
(everybody laughing)

00:08:34.198 --> 00:08:35.863
(cash register dings)

00:08:35.863 --> 00:08:38.479
(jazzy music)

00:08:38.479 --> 00:08:39.644
(Andrew and Steven speak
in foreign language)

00:08:39.644 --> 00:08:41.878
We've eaten a lot of beef on this show,

00:08:41.878 --> 00:08:44.896
but this is some of the
prettiest beef I've ever seen.

00:08:44.896 --> 00:08:46.745
The color is ridiculous.

00:08:46.745 --> 00:08:48.081
Cold-brewed oolong.

00:08:48.081 --> 00:08:49.374
This is one of the coolest things.

00:08:49.374 --> 00:08:51.172
It's like, tea snow globe.

00:08:51.172 --> 00:08:52.730
And it's got the net in the--

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:54.372
- [Steven] No way!

00:08:54.372 --> 00:08:57.542
- [Andrew and Steven] Cheers.

00:08:57.542 --> 00:08:58.375
- Mm.

00:08:58.375 --> 00:08:59.208
- [Andrew] You wanna start with this one?

00:08:59.208 --> 00:09:00.626
- [Steven] Let's do it, the shoulder cap.

00:09:00.626 --> 00:09:02.542
- Cheers, Steven.

00:09:02.542 --> 00:09:03.375
- Whoa.

00:09:03.375 --> 00:09:05.042
- [Andrew] One, two,

00:09:06.165 --> 00:09:07.613
three.
- Wow.

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:08.951
Going in.

00:09:08.951 --> 00:09:10.568
One.

00:09:10.568 --> 00:09:11.787
Two, oh no!

00:09:11.787 --> 00:09:12.755
(Andrew laughs)

00:09:12.755 --> 00:09:14.028
- This smells incredible.

00:09:14.028 --> 00:09:14.861
- Cheers.

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:18.268
- Oh, that's nice beef.

00:09:18.268 --> 00:09:20.656
- We're just getting to
eat really nice steak.

00:09:20.656 --> 00:09:21.965
- Yeah.
- With soup.

00:09:21.965 --> 00:09:24.719
- And you get to eat it the
second it's done cooking.

00:09:24.719 --> 00:09:25.552
- Mm!

00:09:25.552 --> 00:09:27.297
- I'm gonna try the same
piece of meat this time,

00:09:27.297 --> 00:09:28.599
but now dip it.

00:09:28.599 --> 00:09:30.513
Shabu, shabu.

00:09:30.513 --> 00:09:31.346
Ooh.

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:33.973
- Shabu.

00:09:35.989 --> 00:09:37.222
- That rocks.
- Can I get in there?

00:09:37.222 --> 00:09:38.055
- Yeah.

00:09:38.055 --> 00:09:39.084
You should absolutely.
- All right.

00:09:39.084 --> 00:09:40.630
One.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.854
Two.

00:09:41.854 --> 00:09:43.269
- Whoa.
- Three.

00:09:43.269 --> 00:09:44.807
- Like you're baptizing the meat.

00:09:44.807 --> 00:09:46.544
(Steven cheers)

00:09:46.544 --> 00:09:47.732
- [Andrew] The dip is awesome.

00:09:47.732 --> 00:09:48.565
- Okay.

00:09:51.415 --> 00:09:52.340
That's doing it right.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:55.216
- There's two great ways to enjoy beef.

00:09:55.216 --> 00:09:57.130
You either cook it very briefly

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:58.976
or you cook it a really long time.

00:09:58.976 --> 00:10:00.574
This is the best of both worlds.

00:10:00.574 --> 00:10:03.870
The quick cook beef and also
the super long cook beef.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.051
- 'Cause the soup is a 10 to 12 hour,

00:10:06.051 --> 00:10:07.609
steeped in beef bone soup.

00:10:07.609 --> 00:10:08.717
- But enough about beef.

00:10:08.717 --> 00:10:10.800
Pork break.
- Pork break.

00:10:11.953 --> 00:10:13.194
(Andrew and Steven groan in satisfaction)

00:10:13.194 --> 00:10:14.690
- At first this did not make sense to me.

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:17.212
But it's because the beef is so precious,

00:10:17.212 --> 00:10:18.739
it breaks up the flow,

00:10:18.739 --> 00:10:22.101
so I don't just crush my
plate of beef all in one bite,

00:10:22.101 --> 00:10:23.083
like I want to.

00:10:23.083 --> 00:10:26.136
- Well, and also, this
bowl of rice is bringing me

00:10:26.136 --> 00:10:28.447
more comfort than my body pillow.

00:10:28.447 --> 00:10:29.280
- What?

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:31.369
- I've had the same one for over 10 years.

00:10:31.369 --> 00:10:33.892
It's hard to sleep without it.

00:10:33.892 --> 00:10:34.775
- [Adam] Change pillows

00:10:34.775 --> 00:10:35.864
more frequently.
- Wow.

00:10:35.864 --> 00:10:37.259
- No, I wash it.

00:10:37.259 --> 00:10:38.765
- That explains a lot about you.

00:10:38.765 --> 00:10:39.783
- It's like a teddy bear.

00:10:39.783 --> 00:10:41.330
We all have that, like, item.

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.511
- Yeah but now mine is
in my parents' attic,

00:10:43.511 --> 00:10:46.173
because I stopped sleeping
with it after the age of eight.

00:10:46.173 --> 00:10:49.506
- Why would you give up
something that's so comfortable?

00:10:49.506 --> 00:10:51.382
- All right, we're gonna
have the broth now.

00:10:51.382 --> 00:10:54.954
We've finally reached the
soup part of the meal.

00:10:54.954 --> 00:10:57.374
Ooh, the smell though.

00:10:57.374 --> 00:10:58.207
- Cheers.

00:11:00.693 --> 00:11:03.146
- Ooh, that is nice.

00:11:03.146 --> 00:11:05.479
It's not so beefy, actually.

00:11:06.915 --> 00:11:07.748
It's got like--

00:11:07.748 --> 00:11:08.893
- Fruity flavor.

00:11:08.893 --> 00:11:10.321
- Yeah.
- Like, apples or something.

00:11:10.321 --> 00:11:12.947
This is the best way
to close out this meal.

00:11:12.947 --> 00:11:15.456
- Yeah, this nice gentle landing.

00:11:15.456 --> 00:11:17.763
It's like when you have a delicious sauce

00:11:17.763 --> 00:11:20.020
and you want a piece of bread to mop it up

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:21.510
to get all of the sauce.

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:23.972
Here, you just drink the sauce.

00:11:23.972 --> 00:11:27.972
(patrons talking in background)

00:11:30.414 --> 00:11:31.376
- Hot pot.

00:11:31.376 --> 00:11:33.380
- That hot pot was so good.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:37.220
Okay, so we've come to
Taichung for our final soup.

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:40.461
But before we have that, we're
gonna have some cold drinks.

00:11:40.461 --> 00:11:41.294
- That's right.

00:11:41.294 --> 00:11:42.347
We're going to Ten Ren,

00:11:42.347 --> 00:11:44.244
one of my favorite
places in the States, so.

00:11:44.244 --> 00:11:45.694
About to be having it here in Taiwan,

00:11:45.694 --> 00:11:46.642
where it's actually from.

00:11:46.642 --> 00:11:49.990
- So we've got oolong
tea, and a black tea boba.

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:51.038
Confession time.

00:11:51.038 --> 00:11:53.183
I'm not the biggest fan of boba.

00:11:53.183 --> 00:11:54.033
- That's fine.

00:11:54.033 --> 00:11:56.155
- I just, eating while drinking, I don't--

00:11:56.155 --> 00:11:57.578
- Isn't that what soup is?

00:11:57.578 --> 00:11:59.076
- Soup is drinking while eating.

00:11:59.076 --> 00:12:01.286
It's completely different,
don't get it twisted.

00:12:01.286 --> 00:12:02.422
- Cheers.

00:12:02.422 --> 00:12:04.643
(glasses clink)

00:12:04.643 --> 00:12:05.476
Mm.

00:12:05.476 --> 00:12:06.309
- That's what I like.

00:12:06.309 --> 00:12:08.987
Unsweetened, nice ice tea.

00:12:08.987 --> 00:12:09.899
That's all I want.

00:12:09.899 --> 00:12:10.959
Instead of another soup fact,

00:12:10.959 --> 00:12:12.646
we're actually gonna have a boba fact.

00:12:12.646 --> 00:12:13.510
- [Steven] Boba fact.

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:16.761
- Boba tea was invented
in the 1980s in Taichung.

00:12:16.761 --> 00:12:20.317
- Oh, some genius out here put
boba and milk tea together.

00:12:20.317 --> 00:12:21.686
There're controversies around

00:12:21.686 --> 00:12:23.532
who actually invented boba milk tea.

00:12:23.532 --> 00:12:26.103
There's multiple reports
of different people, so.

00:12:26.103 --> 00:12:26.936
- Interesting.

00:12:26.936 --> 00:12:28.963
We're now on our way to Gubami,

00:12:28.963 --> 00:12:30.483
where we're going to see Chef Chen

00:12:30.483 --> 00:12:32.930
to try her beef noodle soup.

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:34.601
- [Steven] The iconic dish of Taiwan.

00:12:34.601 --> 00:12:37.248
- We've had it a few
times off-camera so far,

00:12:37.248 --> 00:12:38.771
just for our crew meals and such,

00:12:38.771 --> 00:12:40.985
and it's usually a very inexpensive dish.

00:12:40.985 --> 00:12:42.881
Five or six US dollars equivalent.

00:12:42.881 --> 00:12:45.454
But today's is going to
be a little more deluxe.

00:12:45.454 --> 00:12:47.585
- It's gonna cost around 30 US dollars,

00:12:47.585 --> 00:12:49.343
which is a lot for beef noodle soup.

00:12:49.343 --> 00:12:51.843
But it's gonna be really good.

00:12:52.856 --> 00:12:56.209
- Gubami is beef noodles
in Taiwanese dialect.

00:12:56.209 --> 00:12:57.636
- Why do you think Taiwan loves

00:12:57.636 --> 00:12:59.294
their beef noodle soup so much?

00:12:59.294 --> 00:13:02.021
- It's fast, and also it's luxury.

00:13:02.021 --> 00:13:05.225
You have a big bowl of
noodle soup and meat.

00:13:05.225 --> 00:13:08.904
I never really see restaurants
can do all three good.

00:13:08.904 --> 00:13:10.288
I wanna do things the best,

00:13:10.288 --> 00:13:13.709
so when I do noodles, I want
to find out the best formula.

00:13:13.709 --> 00:13:15.343
We test with different flours

00:13:15.343 --> 00:13:17.138
for almost, six months I would say.

00:13:17.138 --> 00:13:19.919
We want the noodles to be
al dente in the middle,

00:13:19.919 --> 00:13:23.171
but also the outside can
absorb a little bit the soup.

00:13:23.171 --> 00:13:25.749
We use the Japanese wagyu beef shank

00:13:25.749 --> 00:13:28.380
and also we have a condiment
of smoked bone marrow

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:31.554
and on top of it, we have some
shabu shabu of the beef shank

00:13:31.554 --> 00:13:33.742
to give two different
textures of the meat.

00:13:33.742 --> 00:13:34.932
- What is your background in cooking?

00:13:34.932 --> 00:13:37.075
Like, where did you come from?

00:13:37.075 --> 00:13:39.918
- I learned in Paris and I
traveled to States a little bit,

00:13:39.918 --> 00:13:40.944
and then I come back.

00:13:40.944 --> 00:13:43.898
I started my French
restaurant 10 years ago.

00:13:43.898 --> 00:13:46.554
Very fine dining, it
was my dream restaurant.

00:13:46.554 --> 00:13:48.202
But it's in Taichung, it's very weird.

00:13:48.202 --> 00:13:50.453
I think Taiwan people,
they like something casual.

00:13:50.453 --> 00:13:53.301
I want to do something smaller
and now I have the bar,

00:13:53.301 --> 00:13:54.134
I have noodle shop.

00:13:54.134 --> 00:13:56.268
I always just trying
to do something I like.

00:13:56.268 --> 00:13:57.110
(Chef Chen laughs)

00:13:57.110 --> 00:13:59.264
It looks like very refined,
but I didn't do it on purpose.

00:13:59.264 --> 00:14:02.109
I just trying to make it good,
and then it becomes this way.

00:14:02.109 --> 00:14:02.942
- [Steven] Mm.

00:14:02.942 --> 00:14:04.581
(cash register dings)

00:14:04.581 --> 00:14:05.699
- Look at this.

00:14:05.699 --> 00:14:06.696
That's not soup.

00:14:06.696 --> 00:14:10.238
We have tofu skin, cooked
in some of the beef stock.

00:14:10.238 --> 00:14:13.401
This is the radish with
lemon and olive oil.

00:14:13.401 --> 00:14:15.758
Zucchini, confit in goose fat.

00:14:15.758 --> 00:14:19.421
Some kind of green bean and
beef mushroom deliciousness.

00:14:19.421 --> 00:14:21.739
- I know there's a lot of
delicious stuff in front of us,

00:14:21.739 --> 00:14:24.015
I cannot wait for the soup right now,

00:14:24.015 --> 00:14:26.034
but I will be patient.

00:14:26.034 --> 00:14:29.033
(jazzy music)

00:14:29.033 --> 00:14:30.041
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:14:30.041 --> 00:14:31.280
Hold on the soup.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.193
(Andrew laughs)

00:14:32.193 --> 00:14:33.708
That is damn good.

00:14:33.708 --> 00:14:34.636
(Andrew laughs)

00:14:34.636 --> 00:14:36.097
- [Andrew And Steven] Green bean.

00:14:36.097 --> 00:14:38.164
(jazzy music)

00:14:38.164 --> 00:14:41.937
- Oh, I did not think that
was gonna taste like that.

00:14:41.937 --> 00:14:42.770
- What?

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:44.321
(Andrew laughs)

00:14:44.321 --> 00:14:46.330
- It's a smoky, porky, green bean.

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:47.307
Tofu skin.

00:14:47.307 --> 00:14:49.044
- That looks super juicy.

00:14:49.044 --> 00:14:50.060
And meaty.

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:50.893
Cheers.

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:53.313
- That's the best one.

00:14:53.313 --> 00:14:54.146
- No, this is the best one.

00:14:54.146 --> 00:14:55.238
- No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:14:55.238 --> 00:14:56.071
- [Steven] Zucchini.

00:14:56.071 --> 00:14:57.953
- Confit in goose fat.

00:14:57.953 --> 00:15:00.307
(jazzy music)

00:15:00.307 --> 00:15:01.692
Every time I eat something green,

00:15:01.692 --> 00:15:04.462
I expect it to taste
like a crisp vegetable.

00:15:04.462 --> 00:15:06.751
Instead it tastes like a fatty animal.

00:15:06.751 --> 00:15:07.671
This is awesome.

00:15:07.671 --> 00:15:09.390
- Wow, finally the beef.

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:12.179
(jazzy music)

00:15:12.179 --> 00:15:13.051
- Oh!

00:15:13.051 --> 00:15:16.317
- I'm ready to eat some
beef noodle soup right now.

00:15:16.317 --> 00:15:17.598
- Ooh, thank you.

00:15:17.598 --> 00:15:20.098
All right.
- Smell this thing!

00:15:21.047 --> 00:15:21.880
- Oh...

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:23.334
- I can't believe this.

00:15:23.334 --> 00:15:24.364
I can't believe this.

00:15:24.364 --> 00:15:25.757
- Yeah.
- I can't believe this.

00:15:25.757 --> 00:15:27.267
- [Andrew] This is a $30 bowl of soup.

00:15:27.267 --> 00:15:28.776
- Broth cheers.

00:15:28.776 --> 00:15:31.749
(jazzy music)

00:15:31.749 --> 00:15:32.746
(Andrew exhales)

00:15:32.746 --> 00:15:33.579
- Okay.

00:15:33.579 --> 00:15:35.695
- I didn't think a beef
taste could be refreshing.

00:15:35.695 --> 00:15:36.949
- Yeah, shabu shabu?

00:15:36.949 --> 00:15:40.579
- Yeah, let's do the
choice cut meat on top.

00:15:40.579 --> 00:15:43.052
(jazzy music)

00:15:43.052 --> 00:15:43.885
- Wow.

00:15:45.709 --> 00:15:47.688
- Very flavorful beef, okay.

00:15:47.688 --> 00:15:48.521
- Jeez!

00:15:49.405 --> 00:15:51.124
That is good.

00:15:51.124 --> 00:15:53.667
I literally just ate a
pastrami sandwich in one bite.

00:15:53.667 --> 00:15:54.500
- Yeah.

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:57.172
- And the juices of the
soup just bursting out.

00:15:57.172 --> 00:15:58.267
Inga have some.

00:15:58.267 --> 00:15:59.684
Come, come, come.

00:16:04.881 --> 00:16:06.177
- This is so good.

00:16:06.177 --> 00:16:09.548
(slurping sounds)

00:16:09.548 --> 00:16:11.121
- Those are great noodles!

00:16:11.121 --> 00:16:12.371
Springy, chewy.

00:16:13.633 --> 00:16:15.697
Look at that beef.

00:16:15.697 --> 00:16:16.751
Wow.

00:16:16.751 --> 00:16:19.205
Holy crap, I didn't think it
was going to be that soft.

00:16:19.205 --> 00:16:20.288
What?
- Yeah.

00:16:22.163 --> 00:16:23.858
(crew laughing in the background)

00:16:23.858 --> 00:16:26.781
- It's like softer than taffy.

00:16:26.781 --> 00:16:30.093
Softer than, it's somewhere...

00:16:30.093 --> 00:16:31.783
- You gotta be kidding me!

00:16:31.783 --> 00:16:33.591
- Okay, let's add the bone marrow.

00:16:33.591 --> 00:16:36.636
This is like buttering
already buttered bread.

00:16:36.636 --> 00:16:38.187
(slurping sounds)

00:16:38.187 --> 00:16:39.020
(Steven exhales)

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:40.178
- Gah, whoa.

00:16:40.178 --> 00:16:41.749
Including all the steaks we've eaten,

00:16:41.749 --> 00:16:44.592
this beef, best beef
taste I've ever tasted.

00:16:44.592 --> 00:16:45.476
And the best part?

00:16:45.476 --> 00:16:47.467
You get to eat noodles the whole time.

00:16:47.467 --> 00:16:48.591
It's like usually a steak,

00:16:48.591 --> 00:16:49.569
you're just eating steak.

00:16:49.569 --> 00:16:51.275
Pretty fun, but okay.

00:16:51.275 --> 00:16:53.327
Noodles the whole time?

00:16:53.327 --> 00:16:54.298
(both laugh)

00:16:54.298 --> 00:16:55.830
- Yeah, I've had a lot of
beef noodle soup before,

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:59.513
and it's never bad, it's always
satisfying and comforting.

00:16:59.513 --> 00:17:01.237
But this one is like,

00:17:01.237 --> 00:17:02.888
a boy was born in Akron, Ohio,

00:17:02.888 --> 00:17:04.577
awarded him the chosen
one in an ESPN magazine

00:17:04.577 --> 00:17:05.465
when he was 14,

00:17:05.465 --> 00:17:06.809
turned out to be a
great basketball player.

00:17:06.809 --> 00:17:07.642
- Who is this?

00:17:07.642 --> 00:17:08.475
- LeBron James.

00:17:08.475 --> 00:17:09.566
- Oh, goddammit.

00:17:09.566 --> 00:17:10.797
Every time.

00:17:10.797 --> 00:17:11.669
- Gubami.

00:17:11.669 --> 00:17:14.153
- One of the best soup
dishes I've ever had,

00:17:14.153 --> 00:17:16.037
one of the best noodle
dishes I've ever had,

00:17:16.037 --> 00:17:17.591
one of the best beef dishes I've ever had.

00:17:17.591 --> 00:17:18.424
- I like what you did there.

00:17:18.424 --> 00:17:19.698
- Before we get to our Worth It winners,

00:17:19.698 --> 00:17:22.669
Andrew, what was your favorite
thing that was not a soup

00:17:22.669 --> 00:17:23.636
in this episode?

00:17:23.636 --> 00:17:25.996
- The craft beer at Smart Fish.

00:17:25.996 --> 00:17:26.829
- [Steven] Oh.

00:17:26.829 --> 00:17:29.658
- I never thought I'd see a
beer with a fish soup logo.

00:17:29.658 --> 00:17:31.684
What was your favorite non-soup thing?

00:17:31.684 --> 00:17:32.608
- Beef taxi.

00:17:32.608 --> 00:17:34.212
There's not even a escort.

00:17:34.212 --> 00:17:37.214
Just beef in the taxi, beef out the taxi.

00:17:37.214 --> 00:17:40.235
- Okay Steven, which soup
was most worth it to you?

00:17:40.235 --> 00:17:42.152
- I thought Smart Fish
soup was gonna be my winner

00:17:42.152 --> 00:17:43.008
when we ate there,

00:17:43.008 --> 00:17:44.698
I thought the beef hot
pot was gonna be my winner

00:17:44.698 --> 00:17:45.920
when we ate there,

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:48.555
but Gubami is my Worth It winner today.

00:17:48.555 --> 00:17:52.059
So beefy, just so much
thought put into it.

00:17:52.059 --> 00:17:54.692
- My Worth It winner goes to Smart Fish.

00:17:54.692 --> 00:17:56.754
- Oh.
- Fish soup was crazy.

00:17:56.754 --> 00:17:59.442
Truly one of the most unique
dishes I've ever eaten.

00:17:59.442 --> 00:18:00.859
- Inga and Annie?

00:18:01.785 --> 00:18:02.785
- Gubami.

00:18:02.785 --> 00:18:03.672
- Gubami.

00:18:03.672 --> 00:18:04.707
- What?

00:18:04.707 --> 00:18:06.035
Adam, who's your Worth It winner?

00:18:06.035 --> 00:18:06.868
- [Adam] Gubami.

00:18:06.868 --> 00:18:08.190
(Andrew sputters)
(Inga laughs)

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.048
- I've never been so,

00:18:09.048 --> 00:18:10.798
this is a Worth It first.
- I win today!

00:18:10.798 --> 00:18:12.807
- That's it for Worth It Taiwan soup.

00:18:12.807 --> 00:18:16.194
We have one more episode in
this miniseries coming up next.

00:18:16.194 --> 00:18:17.132
Steven, what is it?

00:18:17.132 --> 00:18:17.965
- Chicken!

00:18:17.965 --> 00:18:20.548
(upbeat music)

00:18:29.888 --> 00:18:31.005
We're in Taiwan!

00:18:31.005 --> 00:18:32.912
We're back with a three-part mini-series.

00:18:32.912 --> 00:18:34.697
Joining us on all of our episodes,

00:18:34.697 --> 00:18:36.153
our friend, translator,

00:18:36.153 --> 00:18:37.600
- [Andrew] Fellow Buzzfeed producer,

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:38.767
- Inga Lam!

00:18:38.767 --> 00:18:40.177
- Taipei! (laughing)

00:18:40.177 --> 00:18:42.974
- We're gonna be seeing some
great modes of transportation,

00:18:42.974 --> 00:18:46.218
some fun games, some tricks, some treats,

00:18:46.218 --> 00:18:47.091
and some delights.

00:18:47.091 --> 00:18:48.640
You know how you know we're in Taiwan?

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:50.155
The beautiful 101 Tower.

00:18:50.155 --> 00:18:51.573
And because it's steamy,

00:18:51.573 --> 00:18:53.181
which is perfect for the first food

00:18:53.181 --> 00:18:56.148
that we're doing in our trip: dumplings,

00:18:56.148 --> 00:18:57.495
a food that's often cooked with steam.

00:18:57.495 --> 00:18:58.328
- Great transition.

00:18:58.328 --> 00:19:00.528
Today on Worth It, we're gonna
be trying three dumplings

00:19:00.528 --> 00:19:02.499
at three drastically different
price points to find out

00:19:02.499 --> 00:19:04.856
which one is the most
worth it at its price.

00:19:04.856 --> 00:19:06.766
- I am so excited to do dumplings.

00:19:06.766 --> 00:19:07.672
- So excited!

00:19:07.672 --> 00:19:09.417
- I feel like we've been
talking about this episode

00:19:09.417 --> 00:19:10.626
since season one.

00:19:10.626 --> 00:19:13.094
- One of my goals this trip
is to brush up on my Mandarin

00:19:13.094 --> 00:19:15.310
because I have the Mandarin
skills of a four-year-old.

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:16.143
(Andrew chuckling)

00:19:16.143 --> 00:19:18.063
My goal is to get it to a five-year-old

00:19:18.063 --> 00:19:18.937
by the end of this trip.

00:19:18.937 --> 00:19:20.156
- That's a very good goal.

00:19:20.156 --> 00:19:20.989
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

00:19:20.989 --> 00:19:21.916
Dumpling Number One.

00:19:21.916 --> 00:19:24.265
- We're going to see Ms.
Liu in her restaurant

00:19:24.265 --> 00:19:25.284
(Inga speaks in foreign language)

00:19:25.284 --> 00:19:26.814
(Steven speaks in foreign language)

00:19:26.814 --> 00:19:27.647
How's that?
- Is that good?

00:19:27.647 --> 00:19:28.578
- Good!
- We're gonna get some

00:19:28.578 --> 00:19:31.161
